 collocation is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It's time to begin.\",\n        \"It's time to start up.\",\n        \"It's time to commence with.\",\n        \"It's time to get started.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It's time to begin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent prepositional phrase correctly modifies the subject?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"After I finish my work.\",\n        \"Because she is tired.\",\n        \"While he was reading a book.\",\n        \"Since they have arrived.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"After I finish my work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Which lexical choice is more precise?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It's a good idea.\",\n        \"That sounds great!\",\n        \"Oh, I see what you mean.\",\n        \"Well, that was an interesting point.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It's a good idea.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the appropriate tense for expressing an event that has just happened?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"She is going to the store.\",\n        \"He had finished his homework.\"\n        \"I was reading a book yesterday.\",\n        \"They have just arrived at the station.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"They have just arrived at the station.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence correctly uses a reported speech with an imperative verb?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"She told me I should go.\",\n        \"He said he was telling me not to move.\"\n        \"They instructed her to leave the room.\",\n        \"It seems like they suggested we should stay.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"He said he was telling me not to move.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which verb form is correct for the given context?\",\n      \"options\": [\n    